  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is either <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"negative 5\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, or <math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The <em>x</em>-intercepts of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane are the points at which the graph intersects the <em>x</em>-axis, or when the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the given equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals 3 left parenthesis x minus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 5 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x minus 14 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 5 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Applying the zero product property to this equation yields three equations: <math alttext=\"x minus 14 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>14</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"x plus 5 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"x plus 4 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 14 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>14</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 14\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>14</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, subtracting <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 5 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 5\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and subtracting <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 4 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the <em>x</em>-coordinates of the <em>x</em>-intercepts of the graph of the given equation are <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"negative 5\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Note that 14, -5, and -4 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>",
